{
 "schema": "fd-ct-mismatch/1",
 "labels": {
  "what": "3b, descriptive response-mismatch closures at the nominal truth, noise-free and signal-only: pseudo-data from a shifted lateral dump (MP-1's species at their D1 +-1 sigma, W2b's whole recoil at +-4%), the unfolding on the zero dump's response; delta is each closure's bias less the zero-on-zero floor; h is the closure half-span, d the data half-span C_resp is built from (3a's for W2b). Shifting the pseudo-data and shifting the response move the result oppositely, so to first order h = -d (an expectation from the closure identity, not a test): the readout compares h with -d, and the residual h + d is where the two constructions differ",
  "construction": "h and d differ in construction as well as in sign: d's data unfolds carry each variant's shifted background template and shifted fakes, are measured at the data's truth and are relative to f (W2b's d to its own delta = 0 chain); h is signal-only, without fakes, at the MC truth and relative to it. A residual h + d can come from these differences. Cross-talk is built beside C_resp and is not in it",
  "not_citable_for": [
   "a bias under the true detector response",
   "a validation of C_resp or of its species sizes",
   "anything about response variants outside the tested species and W2b's scale",
   "a covariance component or a change to the reported matrix"
  ],
  "no_threshold": "no pass threshold is set (docs/analysis-note/app_response_mismatch.tex:22); Joseph deferred the closure's settings on 2026-10-14; the amplitudes are the existing products' own"
 },
